# pdf-brain down: books node and docs-api orphaned by the reboots

Joel reported pdf-brain down via joelclaw CLI and API (2026-08-01).

## Root cause

The typesense-books migration (another session, WIP uncommitted as of this
repair) had moved the docs corpus off panda k8s onto flagg-native services —
books Typesense node on :8110, docs-api on flagg :3838 — and scaled the k8s
`typesense` statefulset and `docs-api` deployment to 0. Both flagg-side
replacements ran as unsupervised ad-hoc processes, and the 2026-07-30 reboot
killed them. The migration's LaunchAgent installer existed but had silently
failed on headless flagg (`gui/501` bootstrap, error 125/5).

## Repair (all verified live)

1. **Books node**: patched the WIP installer (`LimitLoadToSessionType=
   Background` in the plist template, `user/501` domain) and ran it.
   `com.joelclaw.typesense-books` supervised on :8110; both collections
   loaded (662 docs + docs_chunks_v2); health `ok:true`.
2. **CLI env**: `joelclaw docs` reads `DOCS_TYPESENSE_URL` from process env
   only — added the export to `~/.zshenv` (daemons get it from
   `system-bus.env`, which the installer writes). Fresh-shell search verified.
3. **docs-api**: new `infra/central/native/docs-api-start.sh` +
   `com.joelclaw.docs-api.plist.template`, installed as a supervised
   Background LaunchAgent on flagg :3838. Sources `system-bus.env`, leases
   `pdf_brain_api_token` from the secrets store at start (never logged).
   Health verified locally and via
   `joels-mac-studio.tail7af24.ts.net:3838` (the satellite URL).
4. **Panda k8s** (the old API path, also dead since panda's reboot): colima
   VM refused to start on a stale lima `in_use_by` disk marker after unclean
   shutdown — cleared it (marker symlink only; 322 GB datadisk untouched).
   Cluster healed: node Ready, redis/restate/inngest/dkron/bluesky pods
   Running. Installed `com.joel.k8s-reboot-heal` LaunchAgent on panda
   (Background session type — repo plist patched to match) so the heal loop
   finally runs every 180s as designed.

## Flagged, not fixed

- Pod `system-bus-worker-77ff454797-44cjs` on panda: ErrImagePull /
  CrashLoopBackOff for 9 days — a bad image tag from a stale deploy, predates
  the reboots. The older ReplicaSet pod serves. Needs a proper redeploy or
  rollback of the k8s system-bus-worker.
- The typesense-books migration WIP (CLI/search/typesense.ts changes,
  TYPESENSE_BOOKS.md, installer, restore tooling) remains uncommitted —
  owned by its session. My two-line headless patch to the untracked books
  installer and plist template rides along in that WIP, uncommitted. This
  repair committed only the two docs-api assets, the repo heal-plist patch,
  and this note.
- k8s `docs-api` deployment and `typesense` statefulset stay scaled to 0 by
  migration design; retire the manifests once the migration session closes
  out.
